==============================================================================
O15 — fine-ladder residual  (fit-free; two-point exponent; projection, not fit)
==============================================================================
  Delta_N = sum over primes[N:2N] of p^(-sigma) exp(-i t log p)
  g(N)    = |Delta_N| / N^(1-sigma)          (UNCHANGED from O14)
  ladder  : N_j = round(125 * 2^j), kept while 2N_j <= n_primes
  log-N step = log(r) = 0.6931472   (dyadic ladder: log 2 = 0.6931472)
  Nyquist = pi/log(r) = 4.532360   (dyadic ladder: 4.532360)
  gamma_1 = 14.134725, gamma_2 = 21.02204, gamma_3 = 25.010858
    gamma_1 ABOVE Nyquist (14.134725 vs 4.532360)
    gamma_2 ABOVE Nyquist (21.02204 vs 4.532360)
    gamma_3 ABOVE Nyquist (25.010858 vs 4.532360)
  a difference along j is a difference over a log-N step of log(r),
  NOT log(2) — depth-d values are not comparable to O14's unless r = 2.
  consecutive rungs OVERLAP (block is still N -> 2N); that is intended
  oversampling of a function, not a redefinition of it.

